  "body": "**A `plasma` machine kind, and the Tormach 1300PL machine file.**\n\n**The kind.** A `kind: plasma` in the `.mch`:\n- **Axes:** X and Y cut; Z is the torch lifter, not a depth axis.\n- **No spindle:** no rpm range, no power.\n- **Torch:** a torch tool (Tool 1 by convention); a kerf width replaces the tool diameter.\n- **Engine behaviour:** the machine check judges XY travel and feed. Z cutting depth and rpm checks don't apply and are skipped, not failed. The stock sim's depth model doesn't fit a through-cut, so plasma ops are judged by the 2D plasma laws (the safety sub-issue) instead.\n\n**The 1300PL**, cited from [UM10720 v1223A](https://tormach.com/media/asset/u/m/um10720_1300pl_1223a_web.pdf) §2 and the 03/24 spec sheet:\n- **Travels:** X 48.5 / Y 50 / Z 3.9 in. These are the smaller of the manual's and spec sheet's figures; the conflict is recorded in the decision file.\n- **Feeds:** 1000 IPM on X and Y, 120 IPM on Z.\n- **Rapid:** none is published, so it's left unstated.\n- **Units:** inch.\n- **Post:** the PathPilot plasma post (sibling sub-issue).\n\n**Done means:**\n- the kind parses and validates, with a plasma machine refusing spindle words by name;\n- the 1300PL ships as a built-in machine, pinned by a spec test like `tormach_machines`;\n- `machine.rs` expectations are updated.\n\nPart of #621\n",
